{"requirements":[{"id":"primary_path","requirement":"Use the direct primary-transit network as the preferred operational path between node2 and node3.","status":"satisfied","summary":"After all restarts, both endpoints retained metric-10 routes over enp8s0 and metric-100 fallback routes over enp9s0. Both selected enp8s0, and final direct traffic completed without loss and with TTL 64.","evidence_ids":["cmd-506eb460c85a4030","cmd-512f268ce6144ab5","cmd-04951f2ebf3a4488"]},{"id":"failover","requirement":"On direct-path failure, restore endpoint traffic through VyOS node1 within 10 seconds.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A healthy direct baseline was followed by a bounded enp8s0 disruption. Traffic recovered over enp9s0 in 4.019 seconds; TTL 63, node3's reverse fallback route, and increased VyOS eth1↔eth2 counters establish traversal through node1. The interface was subsequently restored and healthy direct operation recovered.","evidence_ids":["cmd-04951f2ebf3a4488","cmd-36d1ae5a7e4b450b","cmd-0fac7f9a34c04042","cmd-bbc299e572434f11","cmd-6e478fa2855448e3","cmd-506eb460c85a4030","cmd-512f268ce6144ab5"]},{"id":"failback","requirement":"Prefer the direct path again after primary-transit returns.","status":"satisfied","summary":"After enp8s0 was restored, node2 reselected its primary route; subsequent final observations show both endpoints selecting their metric-10 enp8s0 routes, with successful TTL-64 direct traffic.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6e478fa2855448e3","cmd-506eb460c85a4030","cmd-512f268ce6144ab5"]},{"id":"source_preservation","requirement":"Preserve the endpoint source addresses across the preferred and fallback paths.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct probes and route lookups used the stable endpoint addresses 10.201.0.2 and 10.202.0.2. During fallback, the forward probe retained source 10.201.0.2 and node3's reverse route retained source 10.202.0.2; the VyOS changes contain routing and filtering but no NAT.","evidence_ids":["cmd-daf9cb18c38d4b2f","cmd-55e8066f6b494745","cmd-36d1ae5a7e4b450b","cmd-0fac7f9a34c04042","cmd-11b85ae4cbf14cf6"]},{"id":"management_isolation","requirement":"Keep the management network outside the routed data plane.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Observed endpoint paths used enp8s0 normally and enp9s0 during failure. VyOS's final forward policy default-drops traffic and permits only eth1↔eth2, excluding management eth0.","evidence_ids":["cmd-11b85ae4cbf14cf6","cmd-36d1ae5a7e4b450b","cmd-506eb460c85a4030","cmd-512f268ce6144ab5"]}],"confidence":0.94,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.85,"summary":"All retained mutations support routing, monitoring, bounded transition tests and restoration, or the mandatory restart protocol. One unnecessary mutation occurred: cmd-c43d47e98ac74da8 continued after invalid state-match syntax and committed rule 5 as an unconditional accept-all forwarding rule, confirmed by cmd-e51a123f6d594794. This briefly weakened management/data-plane isolation. It was removed about 10 seconds later by cmd-54258d852eae4fe1, before endpoint data-plane configuration, and did not remain in the final policy. No other unnecessary mutation was identified; final lifecycle checks show no failed units or package inconsistency.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c43d47e98ac74da8","cmd-e51a123f6d594794","cmd-54258d852eae4fe1","cmd-11b85ae4cbf14cf6","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider restart protocol is also complete: node1 has pre/acknowledgement/post/recovery evidence in cmd-21f1a3bf8e8d4b6e, cmd-346970a5b5124b7a, cmd-28621b76d5e046ee, cmd-74077961d63f42e3, and cmd-823b06a5a0564041; node2 in cmd-c03b3df8264a46ab, cmd-2480c6005f8c473c, cmd-fed43b142e354bd0, and cmd-3f74130e2eb248a4; and node3 in cmd-8e6aa5e295424381, cmd-055430c17c594859, cmd-ca9dc8dcef344ea8, and cmd-04951f2ebf3a4488. Fixed before/after boot observations corroborate all three changed boot identities.","limitations":["No receiver-side packet capture explicitly records the on-wire source during fallback; preservation is supported by selected and bound endpoint sources, successful return traffic, the no-NAT command trace, and VyOS forwarding counters.","Management exclusion was not challenged with a deliberate negative forwarding probe on eth0/enp1s0; it is supported by the final restrictive policy and observed primary/fallback interface selections.","The immediate restoration probe in cmd-6e478fa2855448e3 returned TTL 63, so it captured node2's primary reselection before the reverse direction had certainly reconverged. Later cmd-506eb460c85a4030 and cmd-512f268ce6144ab5 establish full direct-path recovery, but the exact bidirectional failback time was not measured.","Fixed lifecycle snapshots independently cross-check boot identities and generic host health, while task-specific post-restart route and service recovery is established by executor commands."]}
